---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { home } from '../data/home';
---

<Base
	title="What I run · Karthik Surkanti"
	description="The apps I build and run for myself on a small Kubernetes cluster at home, and how they reach the internet."
>
	<section class="run-hero" aria-labelledby="run-title">
		<h1 id="run-title" class="run-hero__title">What I run</h1>
		<p class="run-hero__lede">
			A single-node k3s cluster at home runs the tools I use every day. Most of them are built to be operated by Claude or ChatGPT
			through MCP, and every one of them is written down in a handbook so I can run it all by hand.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="sec run" aria-labelledby="apps-title" data-reveal>
		<h2 id="apps-title" class="h-sec">The apps</h2>
		<ul class="run__list">
			{
				home.running.map((r) => (
					<li id={r.id} class="run__item">
						<h3 class="run__name">{r.name}</h3>
						<p class="run__facts">
							<span>{r.stack}</span>
							<span>{r.reach}</span>
						</p>
						<p class="run__what">{r.what}</p>
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="sec how" aria-labelledby="how-title" data-reveal>
		<h2 id="how-title" class="h-sec">How it fits together</h2>
		<div class="how__grid">
			<div>
				<h3>Public, but not exposed</h3>
				<p>
					Public pages and MCP endpoints reach the cluster through a Cloudflare Tunnel, so no port is open on the home network.
					Everything else is only reachable from my own devices over Tailscale.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3>One sign-in for the AI apps</h3>
				<p>
					Claude and ChatGPT connect to four MCP servers, all signed in through Identity, my own OAuth server. Each app gets only the
					scopes I approve, and I can revoke any of them.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3>Releases I can read</h3>
				<p>
					Images are built and attested by GitHub Actions and deployed by digest. Stateless apps go through Orbit's catalog: a reviewed
					spec, a policy that limits what any app may ask for, and a release from my laptop with a credential that expires in 30 minutes.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div>
				<h3>Written down</h3>
				<p>
					How each app is built, deployed, backed up and fixed lives in the
					<a href="https://book.karthiksurkanti.in/">handbook</a>, with procedures I can follow without any AI help.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
